From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:43:30 +0100
Subject: --interactive, so disparPDFc can show the window

For symmetry with --batch: disparPDFc --interactive is disparPDF.  When
both are given, the last one wins, as with GNU-style options.  Listed
in --help (and so the manual page) and offered by the completions.

Tests: disparPDFc --interactive shows the window and keeps running
(until timeout(1) stops it; skipped without timeout), and disparPDFc
--interactive --batch is in batch mode.  Both fail if --interactive is
not recognized.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DFo7ywK1YasqiQ8A3v7kVX
